virals.hook:
Trump told JD Vance to focus on domestic issues after reports that Vance was considering a meeting with former IRGC chief Mohsen Rezaei. Iranian historian Shahram Kholdi explains what Rezaei’s emergence tells us about who holds power in Tehran. Freedom advocate Gazelle Sharmahd asks why Washington should negotiate with the Islamic Republic in the first place. Whoever gives the orders, she argues, the regime poses a threat to American security and “must be brought down.” You can watch the full episode on YouTube or listen on any podcast platform.

